Multicasting
Multicasting is an excellent feature of delegates. With multicasting, you can assign more
than one method to a delegate. When that delegate is executed, it runs all the methods that
were assigned one after another. Using the + or += operator, you can add methods to a
delegate. There is also a way to remove added methods from the delegate. To do this, you
have to use the - or -= operator. Let's look at an example to understand clearly what
multicasting is:
